{"w": 595.3200073242188, "h": 809.0257568359375, "lines": [{"t": "86", "x": 0.9032117274603759, "y": 0.9742087522985531, "w": 0.03053152114325986, "h": 0.017428414981790374, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "READING", "x": 0.4495901206134314, "y": 0.1526008183429777, "w": 0.13046254235434, "h": 0.023179739115831682, "c": 1, "size": 16.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "READING PASSAGE 1", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.20955823496474332, "w": 0.2852801181661608, "h": 0.023179739115831682, "c": 1, "size": 16.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Frozen Food", "x": 0.4292313304365933, "y": 0.2727601074848447, "w": 0.18425046518134666, "h": 0.026142565890596797, "c": 1, "size": 18.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "A US perspective on the development of the frozen food industry", "x": 0.18850366162746265, "y": 0.30893701644003907, "w": 0.664364161254118, "h": 0.018822616509687834, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "At some point in history, humans discovered that ice preserved food. There is", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3472051993960352, "w": 0.826039169863651, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "evidence that winter ice was stored to preserve food in the summer as far back as", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3753873043976052, "w": 0.82620782341266, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "10,000 years ago. Two thousand years ago, the inhabitants of South America's", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.40371765447174285, "w": 0.8260116931760313, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Andean mountains had a unique means of conserving potatoes for later", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.43204800454588044, "w": 0.8263555618710927, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "consumption. They froze them overnight, then trampled them to squeeze out the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4603783923414106, "w": 0.826055471331306, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "moisture, then dried them in the sun. This preserved their nutritional value-if not", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.48873348764903535, "w": 0.8267271123036813, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "their aesthetic appeal.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.517063837723173, "w": 0.23210252638915418, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Natural ice remained the main form of refrigeration until late in the 19th century.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5553321149826504, "w": 0.826005541678803, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "In the early 1800s, ship owners from Boston, USA, had enormous blocks of Arctic", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5836624650567881, "w": 0.825924649490251, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "ice towed all over the Atlantic for the purpose of food preservation. In 1851,", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6119928528523182, "w": 0.8261205746769721, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "railroads first began putting blocks of ice in insulated rail cars to send butter from", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6403232029264558, "w": 0.8264321480115849, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Ogdensburg, New York, to Boston.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6686906708508241, "w": 0.3532474984167584, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Finally, in 1870, Australian inventors found a way to make 'mechanical ice'. They", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.706810627594949, "w": 0.8260551637564446, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "used a compressor to force a gas-ammonia at first and later Freon-through a", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7351409776690865, "w": 0.826706299738059, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "condenser. The compressed gas gave up some of its heat as it moved through the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7634713277432241, "w": 0.8261746053276272, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "condenser. Then the gas was released quickly into a low-pressure evaporator coil", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7918016778173618, "w": 0.8266147449543113, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "where it became liquid and cold. Air was blown over the evaporator coil and then", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8201320278914994, "w": 0.8265034028544792, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "this cooled air passed into an insulated compartment, lowering its temperature to", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8484624534084221, "w": 0.8264102076714707, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "freezing point.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8768175487160468, "w": 0.15142323090372772, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}], "source": "pdf text layer"}